    "source": "1790 and 1800 census interpolated to 1796, white adults in Virginia, North Carolina, South Carolina, Georgia and Tennessee; only men meeting their state's property or taxpaying rules could vote (Virginia required a freehold). The South Carolina legislature chose its electors, so people there cast no presidential vote."
   },
   {
    "key": "black-south",
